course: dictionary
lesson: 6475
title: Naturally and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Naturally» is an adverb, and it can mean different things. Read the words around it to find which meaning fits. «Many medicines are naturally bitter, so makers add sweet flavours for children.» Here naturally means in a natural way, without people making or changing it. The bitterness is part of the medicine itself.
explain: «Naturally, she was happy.» Here naturally comes at the start, followed by a comma, and it means of course, as you would expect. Leo says it means happily, but swap in «of course» and the sentence still makes sense, so that is the right meaning.
explain: «Swimming comes naturally to him» means swimming is easy for him, without much trying. «Just act naturally» means be relaxed and normal, the way you usually are. Always swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: «Naturally» is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens or why it happens.
fact: «Naturally» can mean in a way that people did not make or change, like wood, wool, rock and honey, which are naturally occurring.
fact: «Naturally» can mean of course: «Naturally, she was happy» means she was happy, as you would expect.
fact: «Naturally» can mean easily, without trying hard: «Swimming comes naturally to him» means he finds swimming easy.
fact: «Naturally» can also mean relaxed and normal: «Just act naturally» means behave as you usually do.
exercise: «Swimming comes naturally to him.» What does naturally mean here? | Slowly and carefully | Of course | In a wild place, like a forest | *Easily, without trying hard
exercise: «Naturally, she was happy.» What does naturally mean here? | In a natural way, made by nature | Very quickly | Without making any noise | *Of course, as you would expect
exercise: «Some foods are naturally sweet.» What does naturally mean? | Easily, without trying hard | Made by a cook | Very slowly | *In a natural way, not made or changed by people
test: «Just act naturally when the camera is on.» What does naturally mean here? | *Relaxed and normal, the way you usually are | Of course, as you would expect | Loudly and proudly | Without anyone helping
test: Ella says «naturally» in «Naturally, the film was late» means easily. Is she right? | Yes, it means relaxed and normal | Yes, it means easily, without trying | No, it means very slowly | *No, it means of course, as you would expect
exam: Choose the meaning of «naturally» in «Wild animals stop behaving naturally when they see or smell people.» | Easily, without trying hard | *In a way that is normal for the animal, not changed by people | Of course | In a relaxed and normal way, as they usually behave
